{
  "description": "Fixed, byte-exact vectors for the device sealed-secret signing preimage (DeviceSealedSecretBundle.signingPayload) and its credential normalization. Every derived value is computed from the keys and inputs only; tests/unit/contexts/identity-devices/domain/DeviceSealedSecretVectors.spec.ts recomputes them with the real domain code, so any drift in key order, purpose, field set, credential form or signature scheme fails. The UI pins the same signingPayload bytes and signature.",
  "algorithms": {
    "signingPayload": "JSON.stringify of exactly these keys in this order: authorizationRevision, generation, identityId, publisherCredential, purpose, recipientCredential, sealedSecret. purpose is pigeon:device-sealed-secret:v1. Numbers are JSON numbers, strings are unescaped base64 or the sealedSecret text.",
    "credentialForm": "Body-only base64 SPKI: the PEM BEGIN/END lines and all whitespace removed (IdentityId.valueOf). identityId, publisherCredential and recipientCredential are in this form inside the preimage and in the stored bundle. The node normalizes PEM input in DeviceSealedSecretBundle.fromPrimitives.",
    "signature": "Ed25519 over utf8(signingPayload), standard base64 with padding (88 characters). Ed25519 is deterministic, so the signature is byte-exact.",
    "keyDerivation": "Ed25519 seed = sha256(utf8(\"pigeon-vector:device-sealed-secret:<role>\")); PKCS#8 private key = 302e020100300506032b657004220420 || seed."
  },
